{"_id":"68a736238ec3d8323af19911","nodeId":"u24UlZKI86vaguj_VpMv1","roadmapSlug":"kubernetes","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:15.590Z","description":"# ConfigMaps\n\nConfigMaps are a way to store configuration data that can be used by applications running in the cluster. A Config Map is a key-value store that can hold configuration data such as database URLs, credentials, API keys, or any other application configuration data that can be used by the application.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"ConfigMaps Documentation","url":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/configuration/configmap/","_id":"6a7f4aadcb44947debcf91bb"},{"type":"article","title":"Kubernetes CRDs: What They Are and Why They Are Useful","url":"https://thenewstack.io/kubernetes-crds-what-they-are-and-why-they-are-useful/","_id":"6a7f4aadcb44947debcf91bc"},{"type":"video","title":"Tutorial - ConfigMap in Kubernetes","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BPrC_lgmcHQ","_id":"6a7f4aadcb44947debcf91bd"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:04:45.052Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04e1fb5fcb94d0416f04","title":"DataCamp - Introduction to Kubernetes","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/R0D14R"},{"_id":"6a5e04e1fb5fcb94d0416f8c","title":"DataCamp - Containerization and Virtualization","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/n4g6RM"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/kubernetes/content/u24UlZKI86vaguj_VpMv1.md"}